  "result": "`src/config/nav.ts` decides it. The `visibleNav()` function there is the only place that filters the entries for a given person. It drops an entry if the entry's feature flag is off. It also drops an entry if `can(actor, item.action, …)` says that person lacks the permission. Roles and plan-gated features enter through those two checks. Nothing branches on `actor.role` directly.\n\nThe other files only feed or consume that filter:\n- `src/components/domain/nav/app-sidebar.tsx` calls `visibleNav()` on the `SIDEBAR_NAV` and `SETTINGS_NAV` lists and renders the result.\n- `src/lib/permissions.ts` (`can`) and `src/lib/feature-flags.ts` (`isEnabled`) supply the permission and flag answers.\n\nANSWER: src/config/nav.ts",
